---
const pains = [
  {
    title: "Agents forget every session",
    body: "Preferences, decisions, and project context die when the context window resets. You re-explain the same things.",
  },
  {
    title: "Flat stores bloat",
    body: "Dump everything into one bag and recall gets noisy. Tokens rise. Signal falls. Memory becomes a liability.",
  },
  {
    title: "No lifecycle discipline",
    body: "Without tiers, scores, and pruning, agents keep stale facts and never promote proven patterns into skills.",
  },
];
---

<section class="section-pad border-0 bg-white" id="problem" aria-labelledby="problem-heading">
  <div class="container-content">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-4">The problem</p>
      <h2
        id="problem-heading"
        class="font-display text-[clamp(1.75rem,3.5vw,2.5rem)] font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-black text-balance"
      >
        What should be remembered gets forgotten, or never cleaned.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-xl text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-500">
        Agent amnesia and unbounded memory bloat are two sides of the same
        infrastructure gap. Nura is the layer in between.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-14 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
      {
        pains.map((item, i) => (
          <article class="panel p-7">
            <span class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">0{i + 1}</span>
            <h3 class="mt-4 font-display text-base font-semibold tracking-tight text-black">
              {item.title}
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-500">{item.body}</p>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
